reviews.text_post_rebuttal_justification:
I thank the authors for their detailed responses. I noted a mathematical discrepancy between the text definition of the Equal Accuracy Gap ((\Delta = \max_k |\text{Dice}
k - \text{Dice}
{\text{overall}}|)) in Section 3.2 and the actual values printed in the table (quantitative results provided in Table 1).
The printed values for (\Delta ) across all datasets consistently reflect the Max-Min Gap ((\max_k \text{Dice}_k - \min_k \text{Dice}_k)) rather than deviation from the overall mean. For instance, in the PI-CAI site baseline, the table reports a gap of 9.8% (exactly (58.1\% - 48.3\%)).
I recommend to fix this discrepancy in the final version.

