reviews.text_contribution:
This paper addresses autonomous coronary guidewire navigation in PCI, a long-horizon continuous-control problem. It proposes CAG-WM, a synthetic-data-driven coronary world model with three main components:
(1) a synthetic data pipeline that generates paired CAG–3D coronary data through implicit 3D generation, segmentation, multi-view reconstruction, and centerline extraction;
(2) a SOFA-based physics simulation for guidewire–vessel interaction;
(3) a TD-MPC2-style world model that performs latent dynamics modeling and planning to output advancement, retraction, and rotation actions. The model is trained on 100 synthetic cases and evaluated on 20 multi-center clinical cases and 10 public cases, with comparisons against SAC, TD3, CEM-MPC, DreamerV3, TD-MPC, and TD-MPC2.

