reviews.text_strengths:
This paper:
1.combines client-level differential privacy with Shamir secret sharing to estimate global label distribution without exposing sensitive statistics—addressing a key limitation of prior methods;
2.proposes a clean mechanism to switch from FedAvg to distribution-aware aggregation, improving stability and avoiding noisy early-stage estimates;
3.provides a closed-form variance decomposition to determine the optimal switching round, offering clear insight into DP noise, sampling, and heterogeneity;
4.specifically targets label skew and strict privacy constraints common in real-world medical scenarios;
5.demonstrates significant gains, especially on highly imbalanced datasets and rare classes;
6.requires only one-shot estimation with minimal additional communication, making it efficient and scalable.

