reviews.text_contribution:
The paper proposes Fact-Flow, a novel framework that decouples visual feature recognition from medical language generation in order to produce diagnostic reports from medical images.
Given a dataset of (Image, Report) pairs, the approach consists of three main stages:
Using a large language model to extract a unified label taxonomy from the reports, which is subsequently refined and filtered;
Training a vision-encoder-based multi-label classifier to predict the presence of each label in the taxonomy for a given image;
Fine-tuning a multimodal LLM to generate reports conditioned on both the input image and the predicted label set.
The proposed method is evaluated against existing state-of-the-art approaches and achieves higher performance across several commonly used metrics.

