meta_reviews.text:
The proposed paper targets at an interesting and critical problem in existing 3D reasoning-based segmentation methods where the instruction perturbation poses great challenges to segmentation effect. The proposed vision injector and seg-local projector appear reasonable to improve the generalization of existing LVM/LLMs under varied instruction levels. All reviewers recognize the contributions of the proposed method and therefore I tend to recommend acceptance.
However, the authors are encouraged to polish the paper:
1) improve the writings of implementation details;
2) validate the diversity and authenticity of the {prompt template} with respect to clincal practice;
3) add more modality and lesion into benchmarking.

